:: A5_start
<<set $act to 5>><<spend 10>>
<<if $trust.tomasso gte 6>><<trust "tomasso" 1>>
The singing is Tomasso. He stands at a door, smiling.

"Did you think I would let Leonardo's boy get lost? Shall we go in?"
<<else>>
The song is old and sad. It comes from far away. You are alone.
<</if>>

[[Open the door|A5_library]]

:: A5_library
<<spend 2>>
<blockquote>You enter a room and your stomach turns. The books are on the ceiling. The chairs are on the ceiling. A table hangs over your head. On it is a cup of wine. The wine does not fall.</blockquote>

Then you understand. The floor is a mirror, smooth as ice.

[[Look closely at the mirror floor|A5_mirror]]
[[Leave the room|A5_page]]

:: A5_mirror
<<spend 1>>
In the real room above you: table, cup, chair, globe.

In the mirror floor: table, cup, chair, globe, ladder.

What is in the mirror, but not in the room?

<<textbox "_guess" "">>
<<link "Answer">><<mirror _guess "ladder|aladder|theladder" "A5_shelf" "A5_mirror_wrong">><</link>>

:: A5_mirror_wrong
<<spend 3>>
Look again. Name each thing in the mirror. Which one is missing above you?

[[Try again|A5_mirror]]
[[Give up|A5_page]]

:: A5_shelf
<<spend -20>><<give "sleeping_water">>
In the mirror, the ladder stands by the far wall. You walk there and touch the wall.

A hidden shelf opens. Candles! A whole box of them. You melt three into yours.

Behind them is a small glass bottle. The label says: //Sleeping water. One drop.//

[[Take it and go on|A5_page]]

:: A5_page
<<spend 1>>
On a desk lies a torn page. It glows like the moon.

Words come up as you watch. The page is asking you a question:

//What do you want more: to be right, or to be free?//

[[To be right|A5_right]]
[[To be free|A5_free]]

:: A5_right
<<heart -1>>
The glow gets weaker. The page seems sad.

Small words come, then go: //Being right is a small, warm room. Many people die in it.//

[[Turn the page over|A5_learn]]

:: A5_free
<<heart 1>>
The page shines brighter.

<<speak "free">>

[[Turn the page over|A5_learn]]

:: A5_learn
<<spend 1>>
On the back, a drawing. A tower. A bell. And inside the bell, a book.

The missing piece of Leonardo's map.

The book is in the Bell Tower. Inside the biggest bell.

<<clue "tower">>
[[Go to the tower|A5_end]]

:: A5_end [autosave]
<<spend 4>><<set $captive to $trust.rook lt 4 ? "Rook" : "Elena">>
You run for the stairs. Then a scream from above.

<<if $captive is "Rook">>It is Rook. "Luca! I am sorry! I tried to sell the mirror to them!"<<else>>It is Elena. Then silence.<</if>>

A calm voice fills the library. It never shouts.

//"Bring me the book, Luca. Or your friend goes into the fire."//

The Grey Abbot.

[[Climb the tower|A6_start]]
